usiness people biting in  saying I didn't know it could taste like  this and so yeah it was just from there  on I knew it wasn't just Stevens  nostalgia there was like really  something there  we're all missing out on yeah how do you  figure out I mean because you have to  incorporate it into every single dish  though so there's a lot of creativity  involved in that process there is for  sure this was an incredible process for  me to like see what the peach could do  and where it could go and really it's so  versatile I feel like it gets stuck in  the dessert category a lot but I have  found that I have loved it in the savory  dishes more than anything like that  pasta salad with that fresh peach taste  and it's got pine nuts it's it takes it  elevates just a simple summer pasta  salad to like a next level and I we did  it time and time again so it's it's  really been a wonderful book and we're  so excited to see it so Steven tell us  about the peach truck how did that idea  come about it really sounds remarkable  totally so we moved to Nashville in 2010  just a state away from where I grew up  and you know couldn't find a good peach  in Nashville go into farmers markets  grocery stores we just couldn't find  anything like what I grew up with so it  was a couple years later in 2012 we both  still had full-time jobs but we decided  to start bringing peaches from my  hometown to Nashville nights and weekend  selling them just to see if you know  really a night and weekend hobby but it  took off well enough that before the  next peach season we both quit our jobs  and said let's see if we can make a life  out of this and thankfully we've been  doing that ever since and first of all I  love that you still have the Georgia  accent Jessica were you actually like  smuggling the peaches out in your purse  originally before you got to this I was  Rihanna yeah yeah it's kind of  embarrassing but I'm also like I know a  good thing when I see it so I was like  hey I'm on the fo